```text
ORDINANCE – 1st READING – Pursuant to Section 2.2.2 Planned Development –
Regulating Plan or Development Master Plan, Section 5.1.3 Official Zoning Map, and Section
5.6.2 PUD – Planned Unit Development District of the Unified Development Code, amending
Ordnance No. 3841 by modifying certain standards of the adopted district, Planned Unit
Development (PUD), for Lots 1-3, Block 1, Lots 1-4, Block 2, (less that portion platted to Pointe
Plaza, 2nd Filing), and Lots 1-2, Block 3, Pointe Plaza; a portion of Lot 2, Block 1, Pointe Plaza,
2nd Filing; Lots 4-23, Block 1, Pointe Plaza, 3rd Filing; all of Point Plaza 4th Filing; and all of Pointe
Plaza, 5th Filing, Cheyenne, Laramie County, Wyoming (located northwest of the intersection of
Gardenia Drive and Powderhouse Road) – referred to Public Services Committee. (Sponsor – Dr.
Rinne)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Re-appropriating the fiscal year 2020 budget of the City of Cheyenne
according to the provisions of W.S. §16-4-112 & 16-4-113.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried.
(#6020)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – To adopt the Certificate of Canvass and Declaration of Results of the
Canvassing Board for the Cheyenne Downtown Development Authority District Special Election
held October 16, 2019.  Motion (per Consent Agenda) carried. (#6021)

RESOLUTION - Authorizing and recognizing the need to return unused funds from the
Mayor’s Challenge Grant to the Grantor – referred to Finance Committee. (Sponsors – Mr. Case,
Mr. Esquibel, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Luna, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Roybal, Mr. Shanor and Mr. White).  Mr.
White advised the item was reviewed under other items for the agenda at the 11/4/2019 Finance
Committee meeting, therefore, provisions of Title 2 of City Code have been met.  Mr. White moved
to adopt, seconded by Mr. Roybal.  Discussion followed and included: the purpose for the
resolution related to public transparency; expenditures above the amount of $35,000.00 go before
the governing body for approval; documentation and process for the resolution; opposition of
proposed funding mechanism for returning unused funds and the importance of returning unused
portion of funds.  Upon inquiry, Mike O’Donnell, City Attorney, explained the 6th “Whereas”
clause related to reconciling funds stating a reconciliation is currently being conducted and the
information will be shared with the governing body when it is completed.  He noted a subsequent
meeting will be held to determine how to proceed.  Interest was expressed by city council members
to be included in the meeting.  Mr. O’Donnell explained the reconciliation information will also
be presented to the public.  Mayor Orr noted she has reached out to council members to meet for
the purpose of discussing the resolution topic noting only a few responded.  Motion carried.  Voting
“yes” – all members of the governing body with the exception of Mr. Case and Mr. Cook voting
“no”. (#6022)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Directing all revenue from City of Cheyenne Contract No. 5902 to be
split evenly between the City of Cheyenne, Solid Waste Enterprise Fund, the Board of Public
Utilities, and the newly established Belvoir Ranch Recreation Special Revenue Fund – referred to
Finance Committee. (Sponsor – Mr. Roybal)

[CA]
RESOLUTION – Certifying the East Dell Range Boulevard/US 30 Corridor Study –
referred to Public Services Committee. (Sponsor – Dr. Rinne)
